# Native tangent compatibility and smooth antiholomorphic projection

The real and complex tangent transitions are compared in the same
original atlas. The resulting native inverse-trivialization compatibility
proves that the actual cotangent Hom-bundle coordinates commute with
antiholomorphic projection. Pointwise projection therefore preserves
genuine smooth cotangent sections and produces actual native `(0,1)` forms.
